cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "token-lattice-ca: a cellular automaton over token space as a black-box measurement instrument for language-model dynamics"
message: "If you use this software or its research record, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vera Zúñiga"
    given-names: "Nicolás"
    email: nicovera@quetru.cl
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicoveraz/token-lattice-ca"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/nicoveraz/token-lattice-ca/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  A ring of token cells resampled in place by a language model's own windowed
  conditional, with common-random-number coupling so that undamaged copies diverge by
  exactly zero and damage spreading becomes measurable. The repository is both the
  instrument and its research record: findings.md is a dated ledger that keeps retracted
  and amended findings in place rather than deleting them. Code is MIT; the prose and the
  record are CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-docs). Note that the ledger includes withdrawn
  results by design — quoting a finding without its amendment misrepresents the record.
keywords:
  - language models
  - cellular automata
  - damage spreading
  - measurement validity
  - reproducibility
